# Psswd Box Release Notes

## 1.0.0 (24 Jan 2025)

### New Features

- Initial release

## 1.2.0 (06 Feb 2025)

### New Features

- Made the password output auto-copy to the clipboard once generated

### Improvements

- Rearranged the UI to make it more compact

## 1.2.2 (06 Feb 2025)

### Improvements

- Changed font family to something more readable
- Added ability for password font size to scale

## 1.3.0 (11 Mar 2025)

### Improvements

- Updated file structure to use `uv` instead of BeeWare

## 1.3.3 (20 Mar 2025)

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed custom module imports

### Improvements

- Removed unneeded variables
- Corrected variables that didn't need self-assignment

## 1.3.4 (31 Oct 2025)

### Improvements

- Reduced the required Python version

## 1.4.0 (22 Apr 2026)

### Improvements

- Removed "High Risk" symbols from the character pool

## 1.4.1 (23 Jun 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies

## 1.4.2 (21 Jul 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies

## 2.0.0 (03 Aug 2026)

### New Features

- Complete overhaul of the GUI

### Improvements

- Updated backend to simplify readability and improve performance

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed the password output box

## 2.0.14 (26 Oct 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies and Python versions

## 3.0.0 (12 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added a Preferences dialog to manage default settings for character types, length, and auto-copy
- Added persistent settings using `QSettings` to remember user preferences across sessions
- Added 12 new themes (Psswd Box Dark/Light, Phaino Dark/Light, Equinox Dark/Light, Catppuccin Mocha/Latte, Solarized Dark/Light, Gruvbox Dark/Light) with live theme switching
- Added an About dialog accessible from the Help menu showing app version, author, and license
- Added SVG icons for password visibility and copy actions within the password field
- Added a dynamic password strength indicator that scales with entropy and adapts to theme colors
- Added "Copy Password" and "Exit" actions to the menu bar

### Improvements

- Completely overhauled the GUI, replacing the fixed layout with a responsive design that resizes gracefully
- Modularized the codebase, moving all UI components into a flat `components/` directory for better maintainability
- Replaced the custom title bar with a native styled menu bar and direct Preferences button
- Moved all styling into a centralized `styles.qss` file utilizing token substitution for dynamic theming
- Added sensible defaults for first-time users (24 characters, all character types, auto-copy enabled)
- Improved layout resilience, preventing widgets from squishing at minimum window sizes
- Updated README badges to reflect the new Psswd Box Dark theme palette
- Updated the app logo

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed password generation logic to properly guarantee at least one character from each enabled pool
- Fixed the visibility toggle not defaulting to hidden on app launch
- Fixed the password input box collapsing and overlapping the strength bar at smaller window sizes
- Fixed window resizing forcing the generate button to the bottom of the screen
- Fixed menu item styling to ensure consistent colors across all themes
